body:
It works for me:
**package.json**
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "tauri:dev": "_HTTP_PROXY='http://127.0.0.1:1087' _HTTPS_PROXY='http://127.0.0.1:1087' _NO_PROXY='127.0.0.1,localhost,192.168.*' tauri dev"
  }
}
```
Tauri cli use [got](https://github.com/sindresorhus/got) as HTTP request library, and use [global-agent](https://github.com/gajus/global-agent) deal with HTTP/HTTPS proxy
https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/blob/48f3768c41a2c68e2e097fcc1ef50e549c1dfb78/tooling/cli.js/src/helpers/download-binary.ts#L5
https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/blob/48f3768c41a2c68e2e097fcc1ef50e549c1dfb78/tooling/cli.js/src/helpers/download-binary.ts#L16
https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri/blob/48f3768c41a2c68e2e097fcc1ef50e549c1dfb78/tooling/cli.js/src/helpers/download-binary.ts#L49-L51

The problem is **environmentVariableNamespace**, and it's the prefix of the [global-agent Environment Variables](https://github.com/gajus/global-agent#environment-variables). so the env variables needs to start with `_` (😱)
@diversoft @kubijo
